    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0645" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg595"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 209.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your cablegram of the 12th instant, inquiring as to the payment of the
                    Caroline indemnity, a copy of which is appended on the overleaf. It has so
                    happened that the payment was made to-day, of which fact I have notified you by
                    a cablegram, a copy of which is appended on the overleaf. I inclose herein the
                    first of exchange (No. 30762), drawn by the Union Bank of Spain and England,
                    Limited, to your order on Messrs. Ladenburg, Thalmann &amp; Co., 46 Wall street,
                    New York, for $17,500 in American gold. As soon as a proper and becoming time
                    elapses I will make the demand for the return of the missionaries in accordance
                    with your instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
